Description: Parse CSS colours and paint them at the target's precision
 Qt SVG read colours with QColor::fromString(), so every colour CSS Color 4,
 CSS Color 5 and CSS Color HDR define beyond hex, names and rgb() (color(),
 lab(), lch(), oklab(), oklch(), hsl(), hwb(), color-mix(), relative
 colours, the rec2100 spaces) was dropped without a word and painted black.
 This parses the whole <color> grammar, keeps each colour in its own space
 in double precision, and resolves it for the painter's target when it is
 painted: gamut mapped (CSS Color 4 section 14.2) where the target holds
 [0, 1] only, kept outside [0, 1] on floating point targets, 16 bits per
 channel or float, and an invalid colour is reported.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS (ORDER 348)
Bug: https://qt-project.atlassian.net/browse/QTBUG-146683
